From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:33:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] feat(android): the desktop app's starter screen on a PC

On a PC the app opened on its own start screen, a phone-style list of
recent files with a floating "+" button, where Collabora Office on the
desktop shows its starter screen: the web UI's backstage view in starter
mode, with the recent documents, New from the templates, and Open.

StarterActivity loads that screen (cool.html?starterMode=true) in a
WebView with no document and no COOLWSD, and answers its messages
(GETRECENTDOCS, opendoc, newdoc, uno .uno:Open, SETDARKMODE) with
DesktopDocuments, opening documents in LOActivity. It reloads when a
document is closed, so the list is current. The launcher's start screen
hands over to it on a PC; phones and tablets keep theirs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
